# The settings of the base, as an env file: one line per flag, uppercased, hyphens to
# underscores, prefixed KIEBITZR_. `kiebitzr -h` lists every flag of the running build and
# every one of them can be set here — there is no second list to look up, because the variable
# name is derived from the flag (ADR 0007).
#
# Only one value is set here, and the other defaults are deliberately not repeated: a copy of
# a default is a value that stops following the binary. The reason this one is written out is
# that it is the only setting whose wrong value fails *everything* while looking like a
# cluster problem — every image ends up as
# kiebitzr_scan_errors_total{reason="unreachable_image"}.
#
# -platform must match the architecture of the *nodes*: it selects which manifest of a
# multi-arch image index is catalogued.
KIEBITZR_PLATFORM=linux/arm64
